        "raw_reply": "MODULE W4Od2m7p42\n\nSEGMENT: 0\n(*\n  A warehouse robot fleet limits how many bots may be simultaneously active\n  in a shared charging zone, coordinated through a compare-and-swap register\n  holding the active count. A dispatcher attempts to admit a bot by reading\n  a snapshot of the active count, and then attempting to increment the count.\n  If the snapshot is stale, the dispatcher aborts and re-read. A bot may\n  leave, decrementing the count.\n  The model tracks the active count and the dispatcher's read snapshot.\n  SAFETY PROPERTY: the number of active bots in the zone never exceeds\n  the zone capacity.\n*)\n\nEXTENDS Naturals\nEXTENDS FiniteSets\nEXTENDS Integers\nEXTENDS Sequences\nEXTENDS Finite\nEXTENDS FiniteFunctions\nEXTENDS FiniteSets\nVARIABLES active, dispatcher1, dispatcher2, snapshot1, snapshot2\nCONSTANTS Dispatchers, Cap\nvars == <<active, dispatcher1, dispatcher2,(snapshot1, snapshot2)>>\n\n\nInit == /\\ active = 0\n      /\\ dispatcher1 = 0\n      /\\ dispatcher2 = 0\n      /\\ snapshot1 = 0\n      /\\ snapshot2 = 0\n\n\nNext == \\/ active' = active\n      \\/ active' = active + 1\n      /\\ snapshot1' = snapshot1\n      /\\ snapshot2' = snapshot2\n      /\\ dispatcher1' = dispatcher1\n      /\\ dispatcher2' = dispatcher2\n      /\\ UNCHANGED <<snapshot1, snapshot2>>\n      [/\\ snapshot1 = active\n       /\\ snapshot2 = active\n       /\\ dispatcher1 = snapshot1\n       /\\ dispatcher2 = snapshot2\n       /\\ snapshot1' = snapshot1 + 1\n       /\\ snapshot2' = snapshot2 + 1\n       /\\ dispatcher1' = dispatcher1 + 1\n       /\\ dispatcher2' = dispatcher2 + 1\n       /\\ UNCHANGED <<active>>\n       /\\ snapshot1 # active\n       /\\ snapshot2 # active\n       /\\",
